<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82018" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιπτῠχ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which enfolds</i>, used in
			pl. in poet. periphrasis, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τειχέων περιπτυχαί</span>
			<i>enfolding</i> walls, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1357
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1241
				</span></i>
			 (parody of <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιῶν ναύλοχοι π</span>.
			their naval <i>cloak</i> or <i>fence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1015
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλων π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
				91
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>enfolding, embracing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιπτυχαῖσι δὴ χέρας προσαρμόσασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					815
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἡλίου
			περιπτυχαῖς</span> in <i>all that</i> the sun
			<i>embraces</i>, i.e.all the world, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1516
			</span></i>.</div>
